0.01: Initial tenkyu release, derived from Orbit 0.06. Use tenkyu as the app ID, source directory, module names and storage filenames. Preserve the Sun-Earth-Moon clock, integrated calendar, place selection and civil-time options. Add Roman I-XII labels twice around the lunar orbit for a 24-hour scale, with 6-12 pixel font size and 1/2/3/6-hour spacing. On first use, copy existing tenkyugi or Orbit settings and events only when the corresponding tenkyu files are absent. Switch the default clock to tenkyu when it was Orbit or tenkyugi, preserving other system settings.
